<title>MEXICO: FORECAST-Mexico 28-day Cetes seen up at 24.53 pct.</title>
<headline>FORECAST-Mexico 28-day Cetes seen up at 24.53 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1996-08-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Interest rates on Mexico's bellwether 28-day Cetes, or T-bills, are seen rising 20 basis points to 24.53 percent, and rates are also seen rising in most other terms, according to a Reuters' survey of 12 Cetes dealers.</p>
<p>Following is a table comparing last week's primary rates versus expectations for this week's auction and the expected change in basis points.</p>
<p>    TERM	LAST WEEK    THIS WEEK'S SURVEY   CHANGE</p>
<p>    28-DAY     24.33 pct	24.53 pct	     +20 bps</p>
<p>    91-DAY     27.59 pct	28.05 pct	     +46 bps</p>
<p>    182-DAY    30.27 pct	30.42 pct	     +15 bps</p>
<p>    1-YEAR     31.00 pct	30.91 pct	     -09 bps</p>
<p>The results will be released by Banco de Mexico at 1830 (2330 GMT).</p>
<p>-- Karina Balderas, Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9554</p>
</text>
